<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Comp Funct Genomics</journal-id><journal-title>Comparative and Functional Genomics</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1531-6912</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-6268</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">18629098</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2447384</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="pii">S1531691203000226</article-id>		<article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/cfg.248</article-id>	<article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Building a Cell and Anatomy Ontology of <italic>Caenorhabditis Elegans</italic>	</article-title></title-group><contrib-group>		<contrib contrib-type="author" corresp="yes"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>Raymond Y. N.</given-names></name><address><email>raymond@caltech.edu</email></address></contrib>		<contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Sternberg</surname><given-names>Paul W.</given-names></name></contrib>	</contrib-group>		<aff id="aff"><label/>			<addr-line>WormBase</addr-line>			<addr-line>156-29 California Institute of Technology</addr-line>			<addr-line>Pasadena</addr-line>			<addr-line>CA</addr-line>			<addr-line>91125</addr-line>			<country>USA</country>		</aff>	<pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>2</month><year>2003</year></pub-date><volume>4</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>126</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>11</day><month>11</month><year>2002</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>2</day><month>12</month><year>2002</year></date></history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2003 Hindawi Publishing Corporation.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2003</copyright-year><copyright-holder>Hindawi Publishing Corporation</copyright-holder><license license-type="open-access" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/"><p>This is an open access article distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.</p></license></permissions><abstract>		<p>We are endowed with a rich knowledge about <italic>Caenorhabditis elegans</italic>. Its stereotyped anatomy and development has stimulated research and resulted in the accumulationof cell-based information concerning gene expression, and the role of specific cellsin developmental signalling and behavioural circuits. To make the information moreaccessible to sophisticated queries and automated retrieval systems, WormBase hasbegun to construct a <italic>C. elegans cell</italic> and anatomy ontology. Here we present ourstrategies and progress.</p>	</abstract></article-meta></front></article>